cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BlazePhoenix-Staking
message: "If you reference or build on this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Mitra
    website: "https://x.com/Sigmacrit"
  - alias: Fable
    given-names: Claude
repository-code: "https://github.com/blazephoenixxyz-crypto/Blaze-Phoenix-Staking"
url: "https://blazephoenix.xyz"
abstract: >-
  A single-asset staking and lending protocol in which the collateral, the
  borrowed asset, and the reward token are the same token, so no price oracle
  exists anywhere in the system. Solvency is enforced per transaction by a
  conservation identity rather than audited after the fact, and is publicly
  verifiable on-chain. Maintenance is fully autonomous, carried by ordinary user
  traffic with bounded gas and no keeper requirement. Emission follows a
  180,000,000-token biennial-halving schedule evaluated in closed form.
keywords:
  - defi
  - staking
  - lending
  - ethereum
  - evm
  - solidity
  - oracle-free
  - solvency
  - invariants
  - tokenomics
